{%- comment -%}
  Snippet: product-variant-picker
  Phase 4, Stage 2. Renders the current single "Size" option as real radio
  inputs that share name="id" with each variant's own id as the value — this
  is Shopify's native mechanism, so the correct variant submits with zero
  JavaScript and no separate hidden id input is ever rendered alongside
  these radios (that would create a duplicate name="id" and break plain
  submission). For a single-variant product (product.has_only_default_
  variant, i.e. genuinely nothing to choose), the picker is skipped entirely
  in favor of one hidden id input, per standard Shopify convention.

  Exactly one radio is checked on load: product.selected_or_first_available_
  variant, matching the server-rendered price/availability state elsewhere
  in sections/main-product.liquid. Sold-out variants render disabled (still
  visible, per spec) — a disabled radio is excluded from form submission by
  the browser natively, so an out-of-stock size can never be added via a
  no-JS submit.

  The input itself is visually hidden (not display:none, so it stays
  focusable/keyboard-operable) and its label is styled as the visible
  "chip", using :checked/:hover/:focus-visible/:disabled sibling selectors
  in theme.css (section 34) for state styling — a standard accessible
  custom-radio pattern.

  Params:
    product         - required, a Shopify product object
    current_variant - required, product.selected_or_first_available_variant
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product.has_only_default_variant -%}
  <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ current_variant.id }}">
{%- else -%}
  <fieldset class="product-variant-picker" data-product-variant-picker>
    <legend class="product-variant-picker__legend">{{ 'product.size_label' | t }}</legend>
    <div class="product-variant-picker__options">
      {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
        <span class="product-variant-picker__option">
          <input
            type="radio"
            name="id"
            value="{{ variant.id }}"
            id="ProductVariant-{{ variant.id }}"
            class="product-variant-picker__input visually-hidden"
            data-variant-radio
            {% if variant.id == current_variant.id %}checked{% endif %}
            {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
          >
          <label class="product-variant-picker__label" for="ProductVariant-{{ variant.id }}">
            {{ variant.title }}
          </label>
        </span>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </fieldset>
{%- endif -%}
